ers/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/x-gtar","state":"uploaded","size":1286991,"digest":"sha256:0da2d771a45c7d74b1795aa42b670c34d995733b27fb84345ab23a64454ff41f","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-12T19:52:28Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T19:52:28Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/ejgallego/lean-vir/releases/download/4.35-rc4/lean-vir-sdk.tar.gz"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ejgallego/lean-vir/tarball/4.35-rc4","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ejgallego/lean-vir/zipball/4.35-rc4","body":"# VIR for Lean 4.35.0-rc4\n\nThis prerelease targets `leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0-rc4`. Releases now follow Lean's\ntoolchain tags: `4.35-rc4` identifies this release, while milestones such as\n0.1.0, 0.1.1 and 0.1.2 remain independent planning scopes.\n\n- Library-prepared browser resources let applications acquire a verified runtime\n  without discovering producer paths or compiling Wasm themselves.\n- Native conversion separates compiler storage descriptions from selected\n  JavaScript value mappings. Closed boundary pairs are shared per package and\n  converted callbacks reuse per-runtime codecs.\n- Options use explicit none/some variants. Export calls use the full Lean\n  declaration name; the old id/jsName export aliases are retired.\n- Resources, callbacks and opaque Lean references have instance-scoped ownership,\n  explicit disposal and tested failure/growth behavior within supported paths.\n- Scalar Float support and updated setup/Quickstart documentation are included.\n- The native SDK installer selects `4.35-rc4` by default for this Lean toolchain.\n  Explicit archive, URL, tag, commit and repository overrides remain available.\n\nOngoing application codec investigations are outside this release. PR183's\nproposed shared-value JSON API is not included; PR228's unlanded work is also\nexcluded. This release makes no new claim of typed FromJson equivalence or\napplication codec performance.\n\nCompatibility: interface manifest12, resource compatibility6, runtime ABI4 and\nbinary package format11. Regenerate programs and deploy the matching SDK/runtime\npair. Milestone labels are planning scopes and do not determine the release tag.\n\nSource: `be01a69de96c49bde7863baf82e3cc4b7cc904fd` (PR262); tree\n`87edfc2f9a05a21ba3222a13189c3fb094ad89d0`, identical to the PR's tested tree.\nThe matching SDK and content-addressed runtime pack are attached to this release.\n"}